High-dimensional dynamic models are being explored in this paper, focusing on variable selection. Initially, the discussion begins with stationary time series models (part 1), before shifting to non-stationary datasets, including finance and healthcare. Key lines of research are identified, including the application of static models to high-dimensional non-stationary time series. Another area examined is the adaptation of static models for high-dimensional non-stationary data, with a special emphasis on sequences. Lastly, the discussion concludes by investigating model-based methods for selecting individual non-stationary series. The paper primarily serves as an introductory analysis, aiming to provide an in-depth inspection and thorough examination of the subject, while identifying promising areas for future research. A comprehensive supplementary document is available, covering additional topics. The paper will be completely rewritten in French for the second part. 

